# P108 on Android: a real throw of the card into its bound and a held drag back, after the app's own FREE and BOUND steps (about 10 s).
# Positions from the swift-cross-ui-tablet36 AVD on 2026-10-19 (2560x1600 px at density 320, 2x): the 40x40 dp
# card starts at x 20-60, y 138-178 and may move along x up to 300 dp.
# THROW: 20 dp per move with 16 ms sleeps (about 1200 dp/s), let go while moving: hard enough to end on the bound
# whatever the received speed, so the card's place after it is known. Pass (logcat [P108] lines): the DRAG release
# velocity equal to the speed over the last 0.1 s of the points as received, the coast frames on the closed form
# within 0.01 pt, and the end on the bound at 300.00.
# HOLD: the card pressed where the throw left it (x 320-360, centre 340 -- not its layout place), dragged 30 dp
# left and held 0.4 s before letting go. Pass: a DRAG release about 30 dp back with velocity 0 and HOLD, no coast.
